1. no freeze: immutability comes from the type
   t = (1, 2); hasattr(t, "freeze")                   False
   type(t).__name__                                   tuple
   copy.copy(t) is t  (an immutable is not copied)    True
   list(t)  (the mutable counterpart)                 [1, 2]
   tuple(list(t)) == t                                True
2. the errors are TypeError or AttributeError
   t[0] = 9                                           TypeError
   frozenset({1}).add(2)                              AttributeError
   MappingProxyType({"a": 1})["b"] = 2                TypeError
   [c.__name__ for c in TypeError.__mro__[:3]]        ['TypeError', 'Exception', 'BaseException']
3. a tuple is shallow too
   nested = ([1],); nested[0].append(2)               ([1, 2],)
   type(nested[0]).__name__  (still mutable)          list
   nested[0] = [9]                                    TypeError
4. no deep freeze; MappingProxyType is a read-only view
   mp = MappingProxyType(d); mp["k"].append(2)        [1, 2]
   d["z"] = 0; dict(mp)  (a view, not a copy)         {'k': [1, 2], 'z': 0}
   isinstance(([1],), Hashable)                       True
   hash(([1],))  (shallow, like freeze)               TypeError
5. born immutable: numbers, str, None, range; a list is not
   isinstance(1, Hashable)                            True
   isinstance("a", Hashable)                          True
   isinstance(None, Hashable)                         True
   isinstance(True, Hashable)                         True
   isinstance(1.5, Hashable)                          True
   isinstance(range(1, 3), Hashable)                  True
   s = "lit"; s[0] = "L"  (every str literal)         TypeError
   isinstance([], Hashable)                           False
6. no magic comment: a str literal is immutable already
   s = "lit"; s += "!"; s  (rebinds s)                'lit!'
   ba = bytearray(b"lit"); ba += b"!"; ba             bytearray(b'lit!')
7. dataclass(frozen=True) has a back door
   c = Config(); c.host = "x"                         FrozenInstanceError
   object.__setattr__(c, "host", "x"); c.host         'x'
   issubclass(FrozenInstanceError, AttributeError)    True
